 {id:'attend',title:'Make the consequential step together.',body:'Stop before an installer writes anything. Steven and Aiden review the exact target, recovery route, and any proposed security changes on this PC. Afterward, prove both Windows and Linux boot before calling it done.',proof:'Attended approval, both boot tests, GPU/network/audio checks, and a working rollback route.'}
];
const refs=[['Omarchy dual boot','https://omarchy.org/manual/dual-boot-install/'],['Omarchy installation requirements','https://omarchy.org/manual/getting-started/'],['Bazzite installation and separate drives','https://docs.bazzite.gg/General/Installation_Guide/install-guide/'],['Bazzite NVIDIA image selection','https://docs.bazzite.gg/General/FAQ/'],['Bazzite desktop and developer options','https://bazzite.gg/'],['Epic Fortnite OS support','https://www.epicgames.com/help/c-34254770/c-38015632/a25107496'],['Microsoft BitLocker status','https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/windows/security/operating-system-security/data-protection/bitlocker/operations-guide']];
export function SetupGuide({entries,onKeep,busy}:{entries:Entry[];onKeep:(draft:Draft)=>Promise<boolean|undefined>;busy:boolean}){
 const [result,setResult]=useState('');
 async function keep(id:string,title:string,body:string,next:string){const ok=await onKeep({kind:'request',state:'candidate',title,body,why:'Keep a reversible PC setup moving without losing the next question.',next_proof:next,source:'anewgam:setup:'+id});if(ok)setResult('Kept in this browser’s field log. Nothing was sent to the PC and no installation was authorized.');}
 return <section className="page setup-page"><span className="eyebrow">YOUR PC / THE WORKBENCH</span><h1>Windows stays.<br/>A new side opens.</h1><p className="intro">Goober, this is an extra way into the same PC, not a demand to leave your games or accounts behind. Keep your familiar Windows side. Build the Saelion side alongside it.</p>
 <div className="privacy-note"><b>Preparation only. Nothing has been installed.</b>This page cannot inspect the PC or change disks, firmware, or permissions. Saved steps are your notes, not verified installation receipts. Windows, Linux, and iPhone browser profiles keep separate logs until a deliberate export/import; automatic sync is not connected.</div>
 <div className="os-choice"><article><span className="tag">FIRST CANDIDATE / SUBJECT TO INVENTORY</span><h2>Bazzite KDE · NVIDIA desktop</h2><p>A gaming-friendly second side with rollback and developer tooling options. For the previously recorded RTX 2060, evaluate the modern NVIDIA image. Prefer the desktop edition rather than experimental NVIDIA Steam Gaming Mode.</p><a href="https://bazzite.gg/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Use the official image chooser ↗</a></article><article><span className="tag amber">ALTERNATIVE / KEYBOARD-FIRST</span><h2>Omarchy</h2><p>The current manual offers a free-space dual-boot installation. Its instructions also call for Windows encryption and firmware-security changes. That is a reason to review this machine carefully, not to switch protections off automatically.</p><a href="https://omarchy.org/manual/dual-boot-install/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the actual install method ↗</a></article></div>
 <p className="fine">This selection is a proposal, not a hardware test. Bazzite documents Secure Boot support with key enrollment; shared-disk installation still has encryption and partitioning considerations. Neither option makes Windows games automatically work on Linux. Keep Fortnite on native Windows.</p>
 <div className="setup-steps">{steps.map((step,i)=><article key={step.id}><span className="setup-number">0{i+1}</span><div><h2>{step.title}</h2><p>{step.body}</p><div className="setup-proof"><b>Next proof</b> {step.proof}</div><button disabled={busy} onClick={()=>keep(step.id,step.title,step.body,step.proof)}>{entries.some(e=>e.source==='anewgam:setup:'+step.id)?'Add another note for this step':'Keep this next step'} →</button></div></article>)}</div>
 <div className="inventory-box"><span className="eyebrow">ON THE PC / READ-ONLY FIRST</span><h2>Three Windows screens, no installer yet.</h2><p>From Start, search for Disk Management, System Information, and Device Manager. In Device Manager, expand Display adapters. Keep disk-size, firmware, and graphics details for the plan. Do not share recovery keys, account screens, or personal files.</p><p>Check encryption in Windows Settings or Manage BitLocker. No encryption option shown is not proof that the drive is unencrypted. When a check is unclear, keep it as an open question.</p><button disabled={busy} onClick={()=>keep('inventory','PC inventory · questions to resolve','Record disk count, sizes, available space, UEFI/BIOS mode, Secure Boot state, graphics model, and encryption status. No personal files or recovery keys.','Review these observations before selecting a target or changing settings.')}>Keep the inventory questions →</button></div>
 <div className="stop-boundary"><h2>The stop line.</h2><p>No full-disk erase of the Windows disk. No formatting its EFI or Recovery partitions. No clearing the TPM. No silent encryption or Secure Boot change. No automatic Windows-volume access from the Saelion side before its purpose is reviewed.</p><p>A second SSD can reduce partitioning risk, but does not replace a backup, correct-drive identification, or a boot/recovery plan. Keep the default OS unchanged until both sides work and the choice is agreed.</p></div>
 <div className="pdd-panel"><span className="eyebrow">PDD / OPEN PUZZLES, NOT FAKE CHECKMARKS</span><h2>What still needs proof?</h2><p>Actual disk layout. Available Linux space. Encryption and firmware state. The correct current ISO. Both boot paths. A bounded Saelion enrollment. These remain open until evidence arrives.</p><button disabled={busy} onClick={()=>keep('next-proof','Dual boot · prove the disk plan','Do not choose an installer target from a guessed hardware layout.','Inspect the PC and write a precise keep-and-change plan.')}>Keep the next puzzle →</button></div>
 <details className="bird-sketch"><summary>Sketchbook: Sae-bird / Blubird</summary><p>A possible little companion: arrives with a useful signal, leaves a clear trail, returns to the same perch. This is a brainstorm, not a chosen name, implemented agent, or new permission.</p><button disabled={busy} onClick={async()=>{const ok=await onKeep({kind:'idea',state:'imagined',title:'Sae-bird / Blubird · sketch',body:'A possible signal-carrying companion. Name and role undecided.',why:'Explore another approachable Saelion presence without forcing it into canon.',next_proof:'Try one small visual or interaction before choosing a name.',source:'anewgam:brainstorm:sae-bird'});if(ok)setResult('Bird sketch kept as imagined, not implemented.');}}>Keep it as an idea →</button></details>
 {result&&<p className="verify-result" role="status">{result}</p>}
 <details className="setup-references"><summary>Sources and preparation receipt · checked 11 September 2026</summary><p>Current official documentation informed the proposal. It does not establish this PC’s current state.</p>{refs.map(([title,url])=><a key={url} href={url} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">{title} ↗</a>)}<a href="/receipts/dual-boot-preparation.json">Preparation receipt · JSON ↗</a></details></section>;
}

